# Keep build-in-public docs and Vercel current

After finishing user-requested work that changes the app or docs, do **all** of the following:

1. Update `docs/confluence-weekly-build-in-public.md` with the latest product changes (see below).
2. Commit and push to `main` so Vercel redeploys.

## Always push when you change

- `src/**`, `public/**` (except see feature flags note below)
- `index.html`, `vite.config.*`, `package.json` / lockfile when needed for the change
- `docs/ui-snapshots/**`, `docs/confluence-weekly-build-in-public.md`, `docs/confluence-attachments/**`
- Snapshot / Confluence scripts under `scripts/`

## Update the weekly build-in-public markdown **and screenshots**

Whenever you ship operator-visible behaviour, UI polish, design variants, or feedback fixes, update `docs/confluence-weekly-build-in-public.md` **and** capture screenshots in the same session:

- Bump **Last updated**
- Add or extend the relevant week / “polish” section with what shipped and why
- Refresh **Current product capabilities** rows when status changes
- Refresh **How to try it** / supported settings / design variants when those change
- Refresh **Known limitations** when a limitation is fixed or newly discovered
- **Add / refresh screenshots** for new or changed UI (see below)
- Do **not** hand-edit content between `<!-- AUTO-SNAPSHOTS:… -->` markers (those are regenerated by sync scripts)

Keep prose concise and stakeholder-readable (build-in-public tone). Prefer appending to the current week’s polish section over rewriting earlier weeks.

### Screenshots with every product update

Operator-visible changes must ship with PNGs in the doc — not prose alone.

1. Add a scenario under the current week in `scripts/ui-snapshot-features.mjs` (use `featureFlagOverrides` when a design variant must be on for the shot).
2. Map it in `scripts/ui-snapshot-doc-content.mjs` (`WEEK_INTERACTIONS` and/or `WEEK_SHIPPED`).
3. Add empty `<!-- AUTO-SNAPSHOTS:week-N-shipped-<key>:START/END -->` markers next to the new prose if using `WEEK_SHIPPED`.
4. Run `npm run capture:current-week` (captures PNGs + regenerates marker blocks).
5. Commit `docs/ui-snapshots/**` + updated markdown with the product change (or immediately after).
6. Prefer `npm run publish:confluence` after capture so Confluence attachments match GitHub raw URLs; then push any sync artifacts.

Skip new feature shots only when the change is purely non-visual (copy, wiring, docs-only). Always refresh overview landscape shots when the game or fixtures chrome changed.

## Workflow

1. Finish the requested change.
2. Update `docs/confluence-weekly-build-in-public.md` and screenshots as above when the change is product-visible.
3. `git add` relevant paths (never `.env` or secrets).
4. Commit with a clear message.
5. `git pull --rebase origin main` if remote is ahead.
6. `git push origin main`.
7. Tell the user the live URL if relevant: https://ncaaf-data-collection.vercel.app

Do not leave finished UI/app work, stale build-in-public prose, or missing screenshots only on disk.

## Snapshots / Confluence publish

After `capture:*`, `sync:confluence-doc`, or `publish:confluence`, also commit and push the generated docs/snapshot paths as above. When the user asks to republish Confluence, run `npm run publish:confluence` then push any sync artifacts.

## Exception — feature flag defaults

`public/feature-flag-defaults.json` only ships via **Confirm & deploy** in the app unless the user explicitly asks to commit those defaults. You may still add new flag keys with safe defaults when introducing a flag.
